From 85fe9beb61c6dad8c08c6ed3baf1d157eaddcefc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy1210 <andy1210@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 19:22:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] render: P030 is opaque

P030 is the packed 10-bit 4:2:0 format a Raspberry Pi 5 HEVC decoder produces,
and what mpv's dmabuf-wayland output passes through untouched. It carries no
alpha, but it is missing from opaque_pixel_formats[], so wlr_buffer_is_opaque()
returns false for every 10-bit video buffer: scene occlusion culling keeps
drawing what the video covers, and anything gated on opacity refuses it.

NV12 and P010, the 8-bit and unpacked 10-bit equivalents, are already listed.
---
 render/pixel_format.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/render/pixel_format.c b/render/pixel_format.c
index c60dd9d..0886fd6 100644
--- a/render/pixel_format.c
+++ b/render/pixel_format.c
@@ -215,6 +215,7 @@ static const uint32_t opaque_pixel_formats[] = {
 	DRM_FORMAT_VYUY,
 	DRM_FORMAT_NV12,
 	DRM_FORMAT_P010,
+	DRM_FORMAT_P030,
 };
 
 static const size_t pixel_format_info_size =
